meta {
  name: XRPC app.thesocialwire.discovery.getSportsEvents
  type: http
  seq: 63
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/app.thesocialwire.discovery.getSportsEvents
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{oauthAccessToken}}
  DPoP: {{dpopProof}}
}

docs {
  preferredIDs optionally limits matching-only followed schedules (maximum 100); empty remains generic. timeZone is the viewer IANA timezone. Response echoes scope. Activity groups precede team/person, competition, and sport interest tiers.
  Use ?teamIDs=<canonical team ID>,<canonical team ID> to restrict schedules to selected teams.
  The filter intersects feed scope before limits; teamIDs= yields no events.
  Up to 500 scoped cached events, with in-progress games and recent results prioritized.
  Bracket sources are reviewed external official links; no graphs or artwork are rehosted.
  Results remain bounded by provider coverage and are not a complete schedule guarantee.
  Optional shared Sports schedules and standings, independent from article ranking.
  Use ?feed=entity:<canonical entity ID> for scoped fixtures and competition tables.
  schedulesStatus distinguishes unsupported/unavailable from successful empty data.
  Each standings table includes its season, source, status, timestamp, and degradation.
  Provider polling requires reviewed coverage, rights confirmation, and credentials.
  Optional row.zone carries provider-reported or reviewed season-specific places,
  with a type, exact label, and source URL. Places do not imply a secured outcome.
  Hide Scores suppresses standings, result indicators, and scores in the clients.
}
